1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:03,150
He was stuck head-down, hundreds of feet inside a cave.

2
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:04,460
He couldn't turn around.

3
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:05,430
He couldn't back out.

4
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:06,700
The rescuers' plan:

5
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:08,420
pull him back up the way he came.

6
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:10,000
Nutty Putty Cave, Utah.

7
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:12,450
November 24th, 2009.

8
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:14,630
John Edward Jones was 26.

9
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:18,140
Deep in the cave, he squeezed head-first into a narrow passage.

10
00:00:18,270 --> 00:00:19,170
It ran downward.

11
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:21,780
He slid in until he was wedged, upside down.

12
00:00:22,010 --> 00:00:24,890
Rescuers rigged ropes and pulleys, anchored into the rock.

13
00:00:25,130 --> 00:00:26,510
At first, it seemed to work.

14
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:28,880
For the first time in hours, there was hope.

15
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:31,490
Then, reports say, an anchor gave way.

16
00:00:31,790 --> 00:00:33,490
He slid straight back into the crack.

17
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:36,290
Rescuers kept working, hour after hour.

18
00:00:36,630 --> 00:00:40,220
After more than 27 hours, John Jones died in the cave.

19
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:43,620
Officials judged recovering him too dangerous.

20
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:47,030
So the cave was sealed with concrete, with him still inside.

21
00:00:47,470 --> 00:00:49,940
Nutty Putty Cave is now his resting place.
